WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.745
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:18.015 --> 00:20.485
(Kang Hoon, Cho Hyun Chul, Kim Jeong Jin)

3
00:23.715 --> 00:25.725
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

4
00:33.625 --> 00:35.165
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

5
00:55.085 --> 00:57.455
(Happy Anding)

6
00:57.455 --> 00:59.125
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

7
00:59.125 --> 01:00.355
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

8
01:00.355 --> 01:01.555
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

9
01:01.555 --> 01:02.755
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

10
01:02.755 --> 01:03.955
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

11
01:29.028 --> 01:30.428
The reason Tae Gu refused...

12
01:31.438 --> 01:33.438
was out of guilt, which I already knew.

13
01:36.908 --> 01:38.338
Because that's just the kind of guy Tae Gu is.

14
01:48.988 --> 01:51.258
All right, next up is Kang Tae Gu from Class Two.

15
01:51.318 --> 01:53.388
The day we first performed together back then.

16
01:53.388 --> 01:55.288
It's a comedy sketch prepared by Han Jun Seo and his friend.

17
01:55.458 --> 01:56.458
Let's go.

18
01:56.958 --> 01:58.158
Hey, wait.

19
01:58.758 --> 02:00.028
Honestly, more than the show...

20
02:02.628 --> 02:05.138
- Hey, that is so corny. - We need to do a chant together.

21
02:05.598 --> 02:06.698
We are a team now.

22
02:08.138 --> 02:09.638
That moment is what I remember the most.

23
02:17.308 --> 02:18.318
One,

24
02:18.918 --> 02:20.948
two, three.

25
02:21.048 --> 02:22.988
- Let's do this! - Darn it.

26
02:24.388 --> 02:25.388
I am going to kill it.

27
02:25.458 --> 02:27.528
(Green Room)

28
02:36.298 --> 02:38.468
(12th Broadcasting Festival Moonlight Paradise)

29
02:55.348 --> 02:56.348
They laughed.

30
02:58.058 --> 02:59.058
The other kids...

31
03:00.158 --> 03:02.258
looked at us and laughed.

32
03:13.538 --> 03:16.068
They laughed. They looked at us and laughed!

33
03:18.138 --> 03:21.208
You are totally a natural on stage!

34
03:21.208 --> 03:22.978
Look who's talking.

35
03:23.348 --> 03:25.078
You're hilarious, you know that?

36
03:25.778 --> 03:27.178
What are you smirking at?

37
03:27.418 --> 03:30.388
- Get over here. Come on. - You sly devil.

38
03:31.018 --> 03:32.688
Acting all innocent like that.

39
03:32.758 --> 03:34.858
- Nice job. - Good work.

40
03:35.328 --> 03:36.488
You did great.

41
03:37.288 --> 03:38.298
Great job.

42
03:41.998 --> 03:45.568
(Driver Kim: Time to go to the essay prep academy. You can't be late.)

43
03:45.698 --> 03:46.768
Wonderful.

44
03:53.838 --> 03:54.878
Hey, Han Jun Seo.

45
03:56.048 --> 03:58.018
You're just leaving? Let's eat together.

46
03:58.418 --> 04:01.018
Yes, let's grab some food. We're a team now.

47
04:07.658 --> 04:08.858
What are we having?

48
04:09.358 --> 04:10.758
Hey, look.

49
04:10.828 --> 04:12.228
What are you guys going to do if I eat it all?

50
04:12.628 --> 04:13.658
Are you kidding me?

51
04:13.998 --> 04:15.228
Watch this. Five at once.

52
04:19.238 --> 04:21.408
Hey, watch.

53
04:21.568 --> 04:23.408
I will order more if needed.

54
04:23.468 --> 04:24.478
- Just eat. - Really?

55
04:26.308 --> 04:28.808
Are you kidding me?

56
04:28.908 --> 04:32.218
- Five of them. - Five? Fine, five it is.

57
04:34.218 --> 04:35.288
Come on.

58
04:35.648 --> 04:37.348
- Don't laugh. - I'm watching. Go.

59
04:37.348 --> 04:39.658
- I'm watching. - Here, watch.

60
04:39.788 --> 04:42.888
- I'm watching, you punk. - Watch. It's five.

61
04:43.888 --> 04:46.228
- Watch. - Hey, look.

62
04:46.228 --> 04:47.558
- Watch. - Yes, go.

63
04:48.468 --> 04:50.428
Look. Hey, watch.

64
04:50.428 --> 04:52.468
- Hey, give it to me. Give it. - Let's go.

65
04:59.238 --> 05:01.048
Jun Seo. Hold on.

66
05:03.178 --> 05:04.318
You smell like food.

67
05:08.188 --> 05:10.288
Thank you, Mr. Kim. See you tomorrow.

68
05:15.788 --> 05:16.988
I am sorry I am late.

69
05:22.498 --> 05:24.468
Professor Choi called.

70
05:24.498 --> 05:25.968
He asked if I would consider thoracic surgery.

71
05:26.368 --> 05:29.068
- And? - I told him I would think about it.

72
05:30.208 --> 05:31.978
Professor Choi is a nice man,

73
05:32.638 --> 05:34.808
but he is not the kind of connection that would help our hospital.

74
05:35.608 --> 05:37.308
Jun Seo, did you have your essay class today?

75
05:38.348 --> 05:40.348
- How was it? - Pardon?

76
05:41.588 --> 05:43.818
Yes, it was good.

77
05:44.518 --> 05:46.158
We covered various discussion topics,

78
05:47.188 --> 05:49.488
and the other students in my group were quite good.

79
05:51.698 --> 05:52.698
Is that so?

80
05:58.698 --> 06:00.868
(Hwaseo High School Photo Album)

81
06:01.038 --> 06:02.908
Father, this...

82
06:02.908 --> 06:06.008
Everyone is born with their own place in life.

83
06:06.738 --> 06:09.278
And I despise people who do not know their place.

84
06:09.948 --> 06:12.348
I hate the vulgarity of those who cling to others...

85
06:12.348 --> 06:13.778
without knowing their place,

86
06:14.488 --> 06:18.218
but I despise the stupidity of forgetting your own place...

87
06:18.818 --> 06:20.758
and mingling with such people even more.

88
06:22.258 --> 06:23.328
Do you have any idea...

89
06:23.328 --> 06:24.998
what that essay class you skipped means?

90
06:25.758 --> 06:29.068
I took the trouble to help you build connections.

91
06:29.198 --> 06:30.828
Is it really that hard...

92
06:31.538 --> 06:33.268
to swallow pre-chewed food?

93
06:35.538 --> 06:37.778
I am sorry. I will never do it again.

94
06:39.908 --> 06:41.078
Wait in your room.

95
06:41.808 --> 06:44.408
You will certainly be punished for what you did today.

96
06:50.488 --> 06:51.488
Ma'am.

97
06:53.218 --> 06:55.558
Tell Driver Kim he does not need to come in tomorrow.

98
06:56.558 --> 06:57.758
Yes, sir.

99
07:05.998 --> 07:08.408
(Social Groups, Math Competition May 17)

100
07:45.338 --> 07:47.638
Hey, Han Jun Seo, let's go to the snack bar. His treat.

101
07:48.078 --> 07:49.108
- What did you say? - Come on.

102
07:49.178 --> 07:50.178
I only lost to you.

103
07:50.248 --> 07:51.348
Pay for your own stuff.

104
07:52.148 --> 07:53.178
I will pass.

105
07:53.248 --> 07:56.618
Look at him play hard to get. You want to get beat up?

106
07:56.618 --> 07:57.648
Let go of me.

107
07:58.018 --> 07:59.058
That hurts.

108
08:05.658 --> 08:06.858
He means stop acting like you are close...

109
08:06.898 --> 08:07.998
just because we crossed paths once, right?

110
08:08.068 --> 08:09.498
What a jerk. Let's go.

111
08:14.068 --> 08:15.808
I thought that was the end of it.

112
08:28.948 --> 08:30.348
(Father: New Message)

113
08:31.018 --> 08:32.488
Here is this weekend's schedule.

114
08:33.018 --> 08:34.288
Report to me after each one.

115
08:34.288 --> 08:35.758
(Multiple Mini Interview, 1-on-1 consulting)

116
08:35.828 --> 08:37.388
(Science Essay Contest, Teacher Kim Min Seok)

117
08:54.238 --> 08:55.378
Hey, what are you doing?

118
08:58.018 --> 08:59.178
It started back then.

119
09:04.248 --> 09:05.618
I just dozed off for a second.

120
09:20.838 --> 09:21.938
Hey, Han Jun Seo.

121
09:23.008 --> 09:24.168
Lend me your gym uniform.

122
09:25.378 --> 09:27.738
Hey, Han Jun Seo. Lend me your recorder.

123
09:27.778 --> 09:29.978
Hey, Han Jun Seo. English textbook.

124
09:29.978 --> 09:31.348
Hurry up.

125
09:32.218 --> 09:33.218
Hey.

126
09:33.218 --> 09:34.788
- Han Jun Seo! - Han Jun Seo!

127
09:36.148 --> 09:37.248
I am touched.

128
09:40.118 --> 09:41.158
Hey, Han Jun...

129
09:48.398 --> 09:51.168
- Where did he go? - Who? Han Jun Seo?

130
09:51.368 --> 09:52.368
Yes.

131
09:52.468 --> 09:54.198
I just saw him heading to the rooftop by himself.

132
09:55.538 --> 09:57.608
- The rooftop? - Yes.

133
10:06.678 --> 10:07.818
Hey, Han Jun Seo!

134
10:23.768 --> 10:24.768
Have you...

135
10:25.738 --> 10:26.738
eaten yet?

136
10:29.538 --> 10:31.238
Did you run all the way up here just to ask that?

137
10:33.478 --> 10:34.578
Well, no...

138
10:35.908 --> 10:37.078
Not just for that.

139
10:38.378 --> 10:39.618
I did well on the exam.

140
10:39.718 --> 10:41.788
I know, you punk. Nobody's saying otherwise.

141
10:42.188 --> 10:43.718
Show off much?

142
10:48.828 --> 10:50.058
What are you doing up here all by yourself?

143
10:52.558 --> 10:53.628
Darn.

144
10:54.868 --> 10:55.998
Doesn't that scare you?

145
10:56.698 --> 10:57.928
Goodness.

146
11:01.468 --> 11:02.468
Right, that reminds me.

147
11:05.338 --> 11:06.338
Hey.

148
11:07.878 --> 11:09.948
Let's put on a show together on the school trip.

149
11:10.178 --> 11:11.448
Just like last time, you, me, and Kim Nam Il...

150
11:11.518 --> 11:12.578
Why do you keep following me around?

151
11:13.678 --> 11:15.548
- What? - Just because we hung out once,

152
11:15.548 --> 11:16.888
do you think we're in the same league?

153
11:19.218 --> 11:20.418
Know your place.

154
11:22.088 --> 11:23.088
My place?

155
11:26.358 --> 11:27.598
Did you just say "know your place"?

156
11:32.098 --> 11:35.438
Hey, are you mad because I keep borrowing stuff?

157
11:35.468 --> 11:36.608
Let me make this clear.

158
11:36.868 --> 11:39.208
I won't waste my life with you guys.

159
11:39.938 --> 11:41.178
So stop clinging to me.

160
11:42.908 --> 11:43.908
It is annoying.

161
11:52.418 --> 11:54.218
And for the finale, we hit them with one more punchline.

162
11:54.288 --> 11:55.358
Not funny. Next.

163
11:55.428 --> 11:57.458
Crazy jerk. Why do I need your approval anyway?

164
11:57.528 --> 11:59.798
- Next. - Hey, what about this one?

165
12:00.098 --> 12:01.798
It is by a river. A guy is all alone,

166
12:01.798 --> 12:04.668
- fishing by the river, and then... - Boring already.

167
12:05.898 --> 12:07.898
He gets a bite. What do you think comes out?

168
12:10.638 --> 12:12.638
And just like that, everything went back to normal.

169
12:20.818 --> 12:21.948
Explain this.

170
12:22.448 --> 12:23.788
(Class Rank: 1 out of 28, School Rank: 2 out of 193)

171
12:23.848 --> 12:26.188
Does this make any sense to you?

172
12:27.218 --> 12:29.058
What kind of family do you think we are?

173
12:29.088 --> 12:32.128
How dare you let someone stand above you?

174
12:32.158 --> 12:34.328
(Class Rank: 1 out of 28, School Rank: 2 out of 193)

175
12:34.828 --> 12:37.128
Do you know what I despise the most?

176
12:37.328 --> 12:39.698
It is that defeatist attitude of yours.

177
12:40.368 --> 12:41.738
When on earth...

178
12:41.868 --> 12:43.708
are you going to make me proud like your brother?

179
12:44.438 --> 12:46.308
- Having ambition... - Father was as terrifying as ever,

180
12:46.978 --> 12:48.878
and the words coming out of his mouth...

181
12:49.408 --> 12:52.478
made no sense to me at all.

182
12:52.748 --> 12:54.078
You should learn to be grateful.

183
12:55.588 --> 12:56.888
How pathetic.

184
13:04.158 --> 13:05.528
I will not let it slide a second time.

185
13:06.598 --> 13:07.598
Leave.

186
13:13.598 --> 13:16.868
Never forget who you are.

187
13:23.578 --> 13:25.878
(Hwaseo High School Trip)

188
13:31.188 --> 13:32.718
I said hair was free choice.

189
13:34.618 --> 13:36.258
Did I say your face was free choice?

190
13:38.898 --> 13:40.898
Who told you to look like that?

191
13:41.158 --> 13:42.268
I am sorry!

192
13:44.468 --> 13:45.468
I am sorry.

193
13:48.468 --> 13:51.208
More than miserable, I felt lonely.

194
13:53.438 --> 13:54.708
Why is my life like this?

195
13:54.908 --> 13:56.148
That won't do. Push-up position.

196
13:56.678 --> 13:58.108
How long do I have to endure this?

197
14:03.148 --> 14:06.318
If I hold out, will it ever end?

198
14:10.128 --> 14:12.228
Hey, how many times have you been dumped now?

199
14:12.828 --> 14:13.928
Twenty-seven times.

200
14:14.458 --> 14:15.468
Hey.

201
14:15.528 --> 14:16.968
Usually, after being rejected that much,

202
14:17.028 --> 14:18.098
wouldn't you just give up?

203
14:18.798 --> 14:21.498
Hey, I am not just anyone.

204
14:22.708 --> 14:26.608
Put some back into it. Drive it in like this.

205
14:26.608 --> 14:30.208
- Harder. - I am doing it!

206
14:30.508 --> 14:32.618
- Darn it. - You put zero effort into this.

207
14:32.618 --> 14:35.218
- Why does it keep... - What is with him? Hey.

208
14:35.648 --> 14:37.288
- I cannot do this to Lee Na Yeon... - Where are you going?

209
14:37.318 --> 14:39.118
I feel too bad for Lee Na Yeon to do this.

210
14:39.218 --> 14:41.488
What is your problem, seriously?

211
14:44.488 --> 14:46.728
What? Isn't that the prick?

212
14:47.028 --> 14:48.228
Where is he going this late at night?

213
14:48.328 --> 14:50.168
Who knows? What do I care?

214
14:55.638 --> 14:57.638
Come on, Na Yeon is about to get here.

215
14:58.008 --> 15:00.278
- Just go already! - Come on.

216
15:00.738 --> 15:02.878
Let us go back. Hey, my bad. I am sorry.

217
15:03.478 --> 15:04.948
This guy, seriously.

218
15:05.478 --> 15:07.378
He is so stubborn. This jerk...

219
15:07.448 --> 15:09.448
Hey, let us go. Hey.

220
15:13.988 --> 15:15.628
Wait, is that Jun Seo?

221
15:26.268 --> 15:27.798
- What is that? Hey. - Hey.

222
15:27.868 --> 15:28.968
Call Man Sik.

223
15:29.038 --> 15:31.408
Hey, Tae Gu. Hey!

224
15:33.478 --> 15:34.878
What do I do?

225
15:35.648 --> 15:36.878
Hey! Darn it.

226
15:39.718 --> 15:43.348
Hello? Sir. Well, you see...

227
15:43.418 --> 15:45.588
The guys... They fell into the ocean.

228
15:45.588 --> 15:47.158
Sir, what do I do?

229
15:47.958 --> 15:49.388
Talk to me straight.

230
15:49.428 --> 15:52.258
- Why did you fall in? - We did not fall in.

231
15:52.498 --> 15:53.598
We were just going for a swim.

232
15:53.658 --> 15:54.898
Who are you trying to kid, you punk?

233
15:54.958 --> 15:57.368
He called me earlier, bawling his eyes out, right?

234
15:57.368 --> 15:58.998
He said you guys fell in.

235
15:59.838 --> 16:01.338
Did I?

236
16:01.908 --> 16:02.908
No way.

237
16:02.908 --> 16:04.768
They were head over heels in love with swimming,

238
16:04.838 --> 16:06.038
or something like...

239
16:06.138 --> 16:07.378
Was that not what I said?

240
16:08.038 --> 16:09.148
Are you kidding me?

241
16:12.018 --> 16:13.678
Seriously.

242
16:14.118 --> 16:15.418
What am I going to do with you guys?

243
16:16.948 --> 16:19.858
Thirty pages each. Write them properly by the book.

244
16:20.588 --> 16:21.758
Do not try to cut corners!

245
16:35.138 --> 16:37.368
Writing lines like we are in middle school.

246
16:37.608 --> 16:40.438
I like writing lines. You do not have to think.

247
16:44.078 --> 16:45.778
You are not going to ask why I did it?

248
16:47.718 --> 16:49.888
We were swimming together, so why ask?

249
16:50.618 --> 16:52.158
What a weirdo.

250
16:53.458 --> 16:54.488
Hey.

251
16:54.718 --> 16:55.958
That is not what is important right now.

252
16:56.028 --> 16:58.458
I just stood Na Yeon up, so I am about to get dumped, okay?

253
16:58.528 --> 17:00.328
Would meeting her have changed anything?

254
17:00.628 --> 17:01.968
Why, you little...

255
17:04.768 --> 17:05.798
What?

256
17:05.868 --> 17:08.138
- You want to go? Let's go. - Let us do it.

257
17:08.198 --> 17:10.768
Do not blame me when you lose teeth and get a bloody nose.

258
17:11.338 --> 17:12.838
- One punch only. - Don't you cry.

259
17:12.908 --> 17:13.908
I won't.

260
17:13.978 --> 17:15.678
If you take this hit and lose two of your teeth,

261
17:15.778 --> 17:17.908
don't you go running home and crying to your mom.

262
17:17.948 --> 17:19.278
(Episode 4: Come Back Home)

263
17:31.588 --> 17:33.028
Are you heading to work?

264
17:33.928 --> 17:36.268
Let's walk together. I'm meeting friends there.

265
17:36.268 --> 17:37.568
That way looks really nice.

266
17:37.628 --> 17:40.338
Let us take that route. That way works too.

267
17:40.338 --> 17:42.268
Did you eat breakfast?

268
17:43.068 --> 17:44.808
Do you know that you are totally different...

269
17:44.868 --> 17:46.038
when you are with your friends?

270
17:47.578 --> 17:49.378
See? You do not even answer.

271
17:50.408 --> 17:52.218
Around your friends, you are all smiles...

272
17:52.348 --> 17:55.218
like a complete goofball, but with other people,

273
17:55.288 --> 17:56.588
you pretend to be nice on the surface...

274
17:56.618 --> 17:58.558
while subtly drawing a firm line.

275
18:00.118 --> 18:03.388
Where did this defence mechanism even come from?

276
18:05.128 --> 18:06.328
I am annoying, aren't I?

277
18:07.398 --> 18:09.498
You are wondering why I am hovering around, aren't you?

278
18:15.038 --> 18:16.668
I am interested in you.

279
18:21.308 --> 18:22.648
Are we having a staring contest?

280
18:25.648 --> 18:28.048
Can you not see me? Excuse me?

281
18:28.148 --> 18:29.348
Can you not see me?

282
18:30.788 --> 18:31.788
What is with him?

283
18:32.588 --> 18:34.858
I am leaving first. Do not follow me.

284
18:42.228 --> 18:43.468
He did not even try to stop me...

285
18:45.838 --> 18:47.468
What is that? What?

286
18:48.168 --> 18:51.038
Excuse me. Hey!

287
18:52.208 --> 18:55.248
- Gosh, look at this. Whose is this? - Move.

288
18:55.308 --> 18:57.448
Please, just put some pants on.

289
18:59.018 --> 19:00.278
Who is it?

290
19:05.618 --> 19:06.688
Jun Seo...

291
19:08.218 --> 19:10.058
Jun Seo was kidnapped!

292
19:22.738 --> 19:24.568
Your clothes are ready next to you.

293
19:35.188 --> 19:37.618
Why are you just sitting here?

294
19:39.788 --> 19:42.428
How can you eat right now? I told you, Jun Seo was kidnapped.

295
19:42.488 --> 19:43.688
They shoved him into a long black car...

296
19:43.758 --> 19:47.028
- and dragged him off somewhere. - Did you see him get dragged away?

297
19:48.798 --> 19:49.798
Well,

298
19:49.868 --> 19:52.868
I did not catch it clearly, but judging by the situation...

299
19:52.868 --> 19:55.838
Then how do you know he did not get in on his own?

300
19:58.038 --> 20:00.078
- Darn it, cover yourself up. - Gosh.

301
20:00.938 --> 20:01.948
Wait.

302
20:02.808 --> 20:04.608
You think he got in on his own?

303
20:04.608 --> 20:05.918
Be for real.

304
20:05.918 --> 20:08.318
Someone who splits rent three ways to live in a place like this...

305
20:08.318 --> 20:10.048
has no business with a car like that.

306
20:12.318 --> 20:13.318
Could it be...

307
20:14.758 --> 20:16.458
Because he was struggling financially,

308
20:16.728 --> 20:18.358
he touched dirty money?

309
20:19.958 --> 20:22.198
There must be a reason we each have two kidneys.

310
20:23.928 --> 20:25.128
Jun Seo...

311
20:26.938 --> 20:28.868
What are we going to do with these sisters' imaginations?

312
20:29.738 --> 20:31.408
What on earth do you watch at home?

313
20:31.538 --> 20:33.138
- Am I wrong? - Yes.

314
20:33.378 --> 20:34.438
Wait.

315
20:34.738 --> 20:38.678
- Then what is it, seriously? - I guess she wouldn't know.

316
20:39.448 --> 20:41.218
Jun Seo is different from us.

317
20:42.018 --> 20:45.088
- He's crazy rich. Filthy rich. - Yes.

318
21:30.328 --> 21:31.998
The ten years we agreed on are up.

319
21:33.898 --> 21:35.568
I heard you already announced your disbandment.

320
21:37.308 --> 21:38.308
Well?

321
21:38.708 --> 21:40.808
How does it feel to have ruined your life with your own hands?

322
21:40.808 --> 21:42.108
I still have...

323
21:42.948 --> 21:43.948
three months left.

324
21:46.248 --> 21:47.718
Go through the proper steps...

325
21:48.018 --> 21:49.588
and join the hospital's management team.

326
21:50.018 --> 21:52.718
It's not as good as three doctors in the family, but we have no choice.

327
21:53.158 --> 21:54.418
You were always interested...

328
21:54.618 --> 21:56.958
- in management from the start. - Father.

329
21:57.028 --> 21:58.698
I'm not interested in working at the hospital.

330
22:01.498 --> 22:03.928
Do you think it was easy for me to sit back for ten years...

331
22:03.998 --> 22:05.798
and watch you live like trash?

332
22:07.398 --> 22:09.068
Either way, I kept my promise,

333
22:09.938 --> 22:11.068
and now it's your turn.

334
22:18.248 --> 22:19.878
Was this place always this big?

335
22:23.088 --> 22:24.748
What's taking him so long?

336
22:25.858 --> 22:27.358
Leave him be.

337
22:28.118 --> 22:29.828
They probably have a lot to talk about.

338
22:31.488 --> 22:33.428
He needs to make a plan...

339
22:34.028 --> 22:35.498
for his life when he moves back.

340
22:40.068 --> 22:41.068
Tae Gu.

341
22:52.478 --> 22:53.478
Hello?

342
22:54.818 --> 22:57.148
Yes. What's going on?

343
22:57.418 --> 23:01.418
I couldn't reach Jun Seo at all. What are you going to do?

344
23:02.128 --> 23:04.188
- About what? - What do you mean?

345
23:04.428 --> 23:07.328
I told you the rent has to go up if you want to renew the lease.

346
23:07.758 --> 23:09.998
- You didn't know? - A renewal?

347
23:10.568 --> 23:12.768
Wait, Jun Seo said...

348
23:12.768 --> 23:14.268
that you'd definitely renew.

349
23:15.568 --> 23:16.838
Hold on, what is this?

350
23:17.368 --> 23:19.178
Jun Seo said that?

351
23:36.088 --> 23:38.798
I spoke with your friends. They said you never told them.

352
23:39.628 --> 23:41.528
I'm putting the place on the market right away, just so you know.

353
23:47.638 --> 23:52.208
(Kang Tae Gu)

354
23:57.678 --> 23:58.708
I'll get going.

355
24:00.578 --> 24:01.878
Don't forget...

356
24:02.648 --> 24:03.748
who you are.

357
24:10.258 --> 24:12.298
I spent ten years running away for dear life.

358
24:15.398 --> 24:16.698
And I'm still here.

359
24:23.138 --> 24:24.168
Back here again.

360
24:27.278 --> 24:29.608
They say he gets summoned once a year...

361
24:29.608 --> 24:31.448
for his grandfather's memorial service.

362
24:31.448 --> 24:34.278
I knew there was something classy about him.

363
24:34.278 --> 24:37.818
He's just completely different from Tae Gu and Nam Il.

364
24:38.118 --> 24:41.558
Because he only ate expensive things growing up,

365
24:41.618 --> 24:43.628
his skin radiates from within.

366
24:44.458 --> 24:45.558
Let me see.

367
24:45.628 --> 24:48.828
Maybe I should take care of my skin a little bit too.

368
24:48.998 --> 24:50.568
It's been so dry and flaky lately.

369
24:50.868 --> 24:52.568
I really need to see a dermatologist.

370
24:53.138 --> 24:54.498
It's so expensive, though.

371
24:54.568 --> 24:57.038
It's not like I'm earning any money right now.

372
24:57.108 --> 24:58.938
Maybe I should look for a part-time job.

373
24:59.038 --> 25:01.908
Are you listening to me? Am I talking to myself?

374
25:02.878 --> 25:03.948
Same as always.

375
25:04.148 --> 25:07.478
Talking to myself and answering myself.

376
25:08.778 --> 25:10.148
Still no word from Jun Seo?

377
25:10.588 --> 25:11.588
Yes.

378
25:12.048 --> 25:13.788
He probably slept there and went straight to work.

379
25:14.518 --> 25:15.858
Isn't this his first time sleeping out?

380
25:20.858 --> 25:22.098
You know, Jun Seo...

381
25:23.168 --> 25:24.668
Not telling us about renewing this place...

382
25:24.728 --> 25:25.968
Don't you have that interview today?

383
25:27.098 --> 25:29.238
Then shut it and eat up, you jerk.

384
25:29.938 --> 25:31.368
Your brother-in-law set it up, right?

385
25:31.368 --> 25:32.408
You cannot be late.

386
25:34.638 --> 25:35.878
You haven't ironed that yet, have you?

387
25:50.858 --> 25:53.198
(Where are you?)

388
26:18.648 --> 26:19.658
Excuse me.

389
26:23.528 --> 26:24.528
Can we talk?

390
26:41.008 --> 26:42.208
I have a favour to ask.

391
26:44.908 --> 26:46.018
About that day...

392
26:47.818 --> 26:48.948
Please keep it a secret.

393
26:49.988 --> 26:51.188
Especially from the guys.

394
26:57.428 --> 27:00.728
If they find out, they will never let me hear the end of it.

395
27:02.468 --> 27:04.168
Once those jerks latch onto something...

396
27:04.228 --> 27:05.268
Don't worry.

397
27:06.368 --> 27:08.568
I won't tell them, ever.

398
27:11.708 --> 27:12.708
Thank you.

399
27:17.108 --> 27:18.508
And I am sorry for getting angry that day.

400
27:18.848 --> 27:19.848
No.

401
27:21.348 --> 27:22.418
Don't be.

402
27:23.288 --> 27:26.018
It was my fault for crossing the line.

403
27:28.688 --> 27:29.688
No.

404
27:30.188 --> 27:31.458
I took it out on you.

405
27:32.428 --> 27:34.558
I am not usually that much of a jerk.

406
27:37.198 --> 27:38.198
Anyway, I am sorry.

407
27:41.138 --> 27:42.268
And honestly,

408
27:43.438 --> 27:44.908
I am really grateful to you.

409
27:46.108 --> 27:47.478
Thanks to you, I feel like...

410
27:48.838 --> 27:51.778
the guys got to end things with at least one good memory.

411
27:55.618 --> 27:56.618
Thank you.

412
27:58.548 --> 27:59.558
Truly.

413
28:02.088 --> 28:03.488
Of course...

414
28:05.128 --> 28:06.398
when you kept following us around,

415
28:06.728 --> 28:08.928
I did wonder what kind of crazy person you were.

416
28:21.438 --> 28:23.308
Did I offend you?

417
28:24.148 --> 28:26.518
- I just meant... - It is not that.

418
28:32.888 --> 28:34.888
I guess I really am crazy.

419
28:36.088 --> 28:38.888
Ever since that day, I have been reflecting so much.

420
28:38.958 --> 28:41.858
To stop bothering you, and not get ahead of myself.

421
28:41.998 --> 28:44.668
I promised myself over and over. I really did.

422
28:44.668 --> 28:47.038
Even now, begging you not to disband...

423
28:47.038 --> 28:49.538
is right on the tip of my tongue.

424
28:50.468 --> 28:51.468
So...

425
28:52.068 --> 28:53.878
I guess I really am crazy.

426
28:56.548 --> 28:58.008
Still, I am going to hold back.

427
28:59.618 --> 29:02.888
Because I don't want to make things harder on you, Tae Gu.

428
29:09.558 --> 29:10.558
Saying that...

429
29:11.288 --> 29:13.328
- is basically like saying... - Still...

430
29:20.168 --> 29:21.168
Even so,

431
29:21.938 --> 29:25.538
just remember that there is at least one person waiting for you.

432
29:25.938 --> 29:27.738
Could you just remember that?

433
29:39.218 --> 29:40.258
All right.

434
29:51.228 --> 29:53.098
Then can I ask you one thing too?

435
29:56.408 --> 29:58.838
Why were you crying?

436
30:02.308 --> 30:03.448
You told me then.

437
30:05.548 --> 30:07.078
You said you understood how I felt.

438
30:10.348 --> 30:13.018
What did you mean by that?

439
30:17.758 --> 30:18.958
Well...

440
30:23.728 --> 30:24.898
I will tell you...

441
30:33.308 --> 30:35.038
If you call off the disbandment,

442
30:35.948 --> 30:38.808
I will tell you then.

443
30:59.598 --> 31:01.698
You are relentless.

444
31:03.208 --> 31:04.208
Fine.

445
31:04.768 --> 31:05.768
See you around.

446
31:06.208 --> 31:08.538
Wait, no, I did not mean we should meet again.

447
31:10.408 --> 31:12.508
- I'm leaving. - Okay.

448
31:22.258 --> 31:23.788
Gosh, I'm late.

449
31:30.898 --> 31:32.328
Don't get nervous. You will do great.

450
31:32.428 --> 31:33.998
You can do this, Kim Nam Il.

451
31:34.638 --> 31:36.038
(Resume)

452
31:36.738 --> 31:38.268
I can do this.

453
31:41.208 --> 31:42.208
Mr. Kim Nam Il?

454
31:43.378 --> 31:44.908
Hello.

455
31:45.248 --> 31:47.218
- Yes, hi. - I am Kim Nam Il.

456
31:47.578 --> 31:49.918
- Have a seat. - Yes, thank you.

457
31:54.458 --> 31:56.328
I've heard so much about you from my brother-in-law.

458
31:56.388 --> 31:57.828
He said you were his closest junior colleague.

459
31:58.088 --> 31:59.088
Right.

460
31:59.398 --> 32:01.058
I have heard a lot about you from him too.

461
32:01.228 --> 32:03.198
He worried about you quite a bit.

462
32:04.698 --> 32:08.338
Well, anyway, thank you so much for giving me this opportunity.

463
32:08.398 --> 32:09.768
I will give it my all.

464
32:10.708 --> 32:13.208
The interview starts at 3pm.

465
32:13.208 --> 32:14.238
Right.

466
32:14.238 --> 32:16.748
Before we head up, shall we take a look at your resume?

467
32:16.948 --> 32:19.878
- Let me look it over for you. - That would be wonderful.

468
32:19.948 --> 32:20.948
Thank you.

469
32:24.148 --> 32:27.488
Thirty-four. You are a bit on the older side.

470
32:28.288 --> 32:31.688
Age is just a number. I get along with people well,

471
32:31.758 --> 32:34.228
- and I am quick on my feet. - Is this all you have...

472
32:34.558 --> 32:35.628
for your work experience?

473
32:36.828 --> 32:39.598
Ten years with Asura?

474
32:40.238 --> 32:44.608
Well, I worked as a comedian for quite a while.

475
32:44.608 --> 32:46.808
Friends from high school and I,

476
32:46.808 --> 32:48.538
- we formed a comedy trio... - This...

477
32:48.938 --> 32:49.948
Let us take this out.

478
32:50.008 --> 32:51.608
(Comedy Team Asura)

479
32:54.348 --> 32:55.448
Why?

480
32:58.048 --> 33:01.218
In a corporate, rather than someone difficult,

481
33:01.218 --> 33:02.828
they hate someone who stands out even more.

482
33:03.158 --> 33:04.988
If you say you are an unknown comedian in your 30s,

483
33:05.228 --> 33:07.628
they just assume you slacked off for ten years.

484
33:08.998 --> 33:11.368
There is no reason to take that kind of risk.

485
33:12.668 --> 33:13.698
Let us take this out...

486
33:14.268 --> 33:17.038
and list more part-time jobs instead.

487
33:17.768 --> 33:19.008
What part-time jobs have you worked?

488
33:23.548 --> 33:24.808
Have you never worked a part-time job?

489
33:28.448 --> 33:29.588
I am not taking it out.

490
33:32.858 --> 33:33.858
What did you say?

491
33:37.858 --> 33:39.058
I said I am not taking it out.

492
33:43.398 --> 33:45.468
It is my only experience and specialty in life.

493
33:45.528 --> 33:46.538
Why should I...

494
33:47.468 --> 33:49.238
leave it out?

495
33:58.108 --> 34:00.348
Does not being famous mean I was just slacking off?

496
34:01.348 --> 34:03.088
Does failing mean I did not try hard enough?

497
34:10.058 --> 34:12.228
I appreciate that you are trying to help,

498
34:12.658 --> 34:13.698
but even so,

499
34:14.558 --> 34:16.498
I do not think you have the right...

500
34:17.968 --> 34:20.498
to dismiss ten years of someone's life so carelessly.

501
34:24.808 --> 34:25.908
Look, Mr. Kim Nam Il.

502
34:26.478 --> 34:29.408
- That is not what I meant... - I am going to keep putting it...

503
34:30.248 --> 34:33.218
at the very top of my resume. So,

504
34:34.918 --> 34:37.518
I will pretend I did not hear your advice.

505
34:40.488 --> 34:42.488
I already paid for the coffee.

506
34:43.288 --> 34:45.028
Sorry for wasting your time.

507
35:10.248 --> 35:12.248
You do not even have anywhere to go, idiot.

508
35:12.248 --> 35:13.288
Darn it.

509
35:40.778 --> 35:42.848
Hey, this is our debut outfit.

510
35:42.988 --> 35:45.188
What does that matter now? It's over anyway.

511
35:45.348 --> 35:47.988
- It's just garbage now. - Seriously, man.

512
35:48.058 --> 35:49.958
Are you money-crazy? Just sell your own stuff, darn it.

513
36:03.338 --> 36:05.538
- You are back. - You are home early.

514
36:07.738 --> 36:09.278
How did the interview go?

515
36:12.978 --> 36:13.978
Bombed it.

516
36:14.748 --> 36:15.978
I had a sudden stomach emergency,

517
36:16.048 --> 36:17.788
so I was a bit late, and they told me to leave.

518
36:18.288 --> 36:20.258
This world is so harsh, Tae Gu.

519
36:20.358 --> 36:22.018
You should have held it in, you jerk.

520
36:22.088 --> 36:23.128
You know how it is.

521
36:23.328 --> 36:26.028
Whenever I get nervous, my bowels give out first.

522
36:26.428 --> 36:28.028
Come here. Let me plug it up for you.

523
36:28.198 --> 36:30.098
- Hold on. Stop it, man. - Come here.

524
36:30.168 --> 36:32.298
Hey, hold on. I got a call.

525
36:32.598 --> 36:34.338
- It is Man Deuk. - Man Sik?

526
36:35.098 --> 36:36.968
Hello? Yes, Mr. Jung.

527
36:38.068 --> 36:39.068
What?

528
36:40.078 --> 36:41.408
Jun Seo?

529
36:42.378 --> 36:44.378
Is he not working his shift right now?

530
36:46.918 --> 36:48.078
So close.

531
36:48.078 --> 36:50.048
I really thought I could get it today.

532
36:50.118 --> 36:51.618
It wasn't even close.

533
36:51.818 --> 36:53.658
How long are you going to keep doing this?

534
36:54.118 --> 36:55.958
Until I win the giant plushie.

535
36:56.828 --> 36:58.788
It feels like a haunted house. It creeps me out...

536
36:58.858 --> 37:00.258
every time I go to the bathroom at night.

537
37:00.328 --> 37:01.558
- These do? - Yes!

538
37:01.558 --> 37:02.628
There are too many eyes staring at me.

539
37:02.628 --> 37:04.268
One would be fine, but there are so many.

540
37:04.468 --> 37:05.868
I might just throw them all out.

541
37:06.368 --> 37:07.598
I think they are adorable.

542
37:08.568 --> 37:09.808
Darn it, where did he go?

543
37:11.008 --> 37:13.138
This is weird. Skipping work and ghosting us...

544
37:13.578 --> 37:14.578
like someone irresponsible...

545
37:14.838 --> 37:16.348
That is not like him at all.

546
37:16.978 --> 37:18.278
Who is ghosting you?

547
37:19.548 --> 37:22.518
- What? - Jun Seo? You cannot reach him?

548
37:22.818 --> 37:24.488
Ever since he went to his parents' yesterday,

549
37:24.548 --> 37:27.018
he has not been answering his phone. He did not come home either.

550
37:28.288 --> 37:29.358
He did not come home?

551
37:29.758 --> 37:30.758
No.

552
37:31.458 --> 37:32.828
That cannot be right.

553
37:33.128 --> 37:35.798
- I saw Jun Seo last night. - The number you have dialled...

554
37:35.858 --> 37:37.798
He came right outside the house.

555
37:39.268 --> 37:41.468
- Outside the house? - Are you sure?

556
37:42.238 --> 37:43.908
Yes, I'm sure.

557
37:47.738 --> 37:49.578
Where would Jun Seo even go?

558
37:50.648 --> 37:52.908
- The number you have dialled... - Why wouldn't he pick up?

559
37:54.578 --> 37:58.618
Why isn't he checking his texts? Come on.

560
37:58.848 --> 38:00.288
I don't get it.

561
38:00.358 --> 38:02.618
Why come all the way to the house and just leave?

562
38:03.388 --> 38:04.828
Isn't it obvious?

563
38:06.958 --> 38:09.668
He left because he couldn't stand someone.

564
38:10.028 --> 38:12.528
Did you ever apologize to Jun Seo after that fight?

565
38:12.598 --> 38:13.668
You didn't, right?

566
38:15.598 --> 38:16.608
Darn.

567
38:16.668 --> 38:18.068
I told you we shouldn't have brought her.

568
38:20.108 --> 38:22.608
Hey, didn't you say you were heading to an appointment...

569
38:22.678 --> 38:24.108
and asked to be dropped off by the main road?

570
38:24.178 --> 38:25.448
Does my appointment matter right now?

571
38:26.578 --> 38:27.778
I'll help too.

572
38:28.318 --> 38:29.618
Just the two of you searching all of Daehangno?

573
38:29.688 --> 38:30.888
That'll take forever.

574
38:31.618 --> 38:34.358
Look, we appreciate the thought,

575
38:34.988 --> 38:36.328
but you really don't have to do this.

576
38:36.728 --> 38:38.358
We'll drop you off at the bus stop over there.

577
38:38.358 --> 38:39.998
I like Jun Seo.

578
38:42.558 --> 38:44.198
So that makes it okay for me to do this, right?

579
38:55.638 --> 38:57.148
The texture is amazing.

580
38:58.248 --> 38:59.718
- Here. - Cheers.

581
39:12.458 --> 39:16.398
(Comedy Town)

582
39:18.198 --> 39:19.868
Where to next? Where are we going now?

583
39:20.068 --> 39:22.838
I think we checked everywhere he might go. Right?

584
39:22.838 --> 39:25.508
- Yes. - What? That's it?

585
39:26.108 --> 39:27.308
What about people to call?

586
39:27.378 --> 39:28.878
Doesn't he have any other friends besides you two?

587
39:31.448 --> 39:33.008
I asked if he has other friends.

588
39:33.548 --> 39:36.488
Listen, we're all Jun Seo has.

589
39:39.548 --> 39:40.758
Seriously?

590
39:41.258 --> 39:43.258
His life is so boring.

591
39:44.058 --> 39:45.928
Jun Seo's dad's hospital was around here, right?

592
39:48.598 --> 39:50.498
(Yechan Hospital)

593
39:50.568 --> 39:53.028
I'm feeling a little intimidated.

594
39:54.598 --> 39:56.038
This is a private practice, right?

595
40:00.838 --> 40:01.838
Let's go.

596
40:08.278 --> 40:10.848
Are hospitals supposed to have this many security cameras?

597
40:12.018 --> 40:13.618
When is he going to see us?

598
40:17.158 --> 40:18.188
Excuse me.

599
40:18.358 --> 40:20.128
The director is in his office, right?

600
40:20.928 --> 40:24.128
Yes, he's currently preparing for a TV interview.

601
40:24.228 --> 40:25.628
He'll call you in as soon as it's over.

602
40:25.728 --> 40:28.198
His own son is missing, and he's doing an interview?

603
40:29.668 --> 40:31.368
- I can't take this. - Wait.

604
40:32.268 --> 40:34.708
Can I help you?

605
40:37.478 --> 40:38.478
Hello, sir.

606
40:39.108 --> 40:42.318
It's an honour to meet you. I'm Kang Tae Gu, Jun Seo's friend.

607
40:42.848 --> 40:44.988
- I'm Kim Nam Il. - I'm Go Ji Young.

608
40:45.888 --> 40:47.618
You're much more handsome...

609
40:48.388 --> 40:49.418
than on TV.

610
40:52.328 --> 40:53.858
We haven't been able to reach Jun Seo.

611
40:54.328 --> 40:56.458
We checked everywhere we could think of,

612
40:56.528 --> 40:57.828
- and we're worried... - And?

613
41:02.938 --> 41:04.008
So...

614
41:07.278 --> 41:09.138
we were wondering if you had an idea where he might be.

615
41:09.208 --> 41:11.678
I don't. Satisfied?

616
41:12.348 --> 41:13.678
Please leave now.

617
41:13.678 --> 41:14.848
(Yechan Hospital)

618
41:17.748 --> 41:19.318
Excuse me, mister!

619
41:22.858 --> 41:25.258
I've been listening to you, and you're being a real jerk.

620
41:25.488 --> 41:27.858
Jun Seo is missing. He's your brother.

621
41:30.198 --> 41:31.228
Let go of me.

622
41:35.198 --> 41:36.438
Yesterday, Jun Seo...

623
41:38.238 --> 41:40.008
told our father something.

624
41:42.038 --> 41:44.248
Father, Professor Hwang is on the phone.

625
41:45.348 --> 41:46.348
All right.

626
41:50.348 --> 41:51.518
Who am I?

627
41:59.788 --> 42:01.128
Tell me, Father.

628
42:03.298 --> 42:05.968
- What? - If you're talking about your son,

629
42:07.038 --> 42:09.298
I gave up that spot ten years ago.

630
42:10.768 --> 42:12.268
They're my only family.

631
42:13.308 --> 42:14.638
Over my dead body...

632
42:14.738 --> 42:15.808
will I ever set foot in this house again.

633
42:27.888 --> 42:29.018
Do you get it now?

634
42:29.358 --> 42:31.428
Do you see how pointless doing this here is?

635
42:35.028 --> 42:36.058
Excuse me.

636
42:36.928 --> 42:39.798
The director said he's too busy to see you,

637
42:39.868 --> 42:41.068
so please leave.

638
42:46.408 --> 42:48.838
It's all a lie. All of it!

639
42:49.738 --> 42:52.878
On TV, he acts like some noble soul driven...

640
42:52.978 --> 42:54.748
purely by a doctor's sense of duty.

641
42:55.018 --> 42:58.148
His own son goes missing, and what? An interview?

642
42:59.488 --> 43:00.818
I can see clear as day...

643
43:00.818 --> 43:03.058
how Jun Seo was treated growing up in that house.

644
43:03.118 --> 43:04.588
It's a miracle he didn't lose his mind.

645
43:04.658 --> 43:06.558
I would've gone crazy a long time ago!

646
43:10.228 --> 43:12.728
- Calm down. - Where have you looked?

647
43:13.168 --> 43:14.168
Everywhere.

648
43:14.798 --> 43:16.468
Places we've been, places he might go...

649
43:16.598 --> 43:17.968
We went pretty much everywhere.

650
43:18.168 --> 43:20.878
What about there? Back on that school trip,

651
43:21.478 --> 43:22.908
you wrote 30 lucky letters of apology.

652
43:32.788 --> 43:34.058
What? Wait...

653
43:34.318 --> 43:36.958
What? Where are you going? Take me with you.

654
43:37.028 --> 43:38.358
- I said, take me with you. - Hey.

655
43:39.328 --> 43:42.258
- What? What are you doing? - Safe travels.

656
43:44.198 --> 43:46.598
- Let me go. - Gosh, that hurts.

657
43:48.798 --> 43:50.108
I wanted to go with them.

658
43:51.538 --> 43:52.768
Darn it.

659
43:54.008 --> 43:55.878
I knew he was having a hard time.

660
43:55.878 --> 43:58.948
Still, I thought if he lived away from us,

661
43:58.948 --> 44:00.718
he'd be 100 times better off.

662
44:00.978 --> 44:02.978
That's why I pretended not to notice.

663
44:04.288 --> 44:05.288
Hey.

664
44:06.448 --> 44:08.488
What if he's thinking of doing something crazy,

665
44:08.488 --> 44:10.158
- like that time? - Do you have to jinx it?

666
44:10.158 --> 44:13.458
He said he'd rather die than go back home.

667
44:13.458 --> 44:14.598
It's not that!

668
44:15.298 --> 44:16.868
We're not going there to find him.

669
44:16.928 --> 44:18.698
We're going to confirm that he isn't there.

670
44:19.098 --> 44:20.768
If you're going to talk nonsense, shut it and go to sleep.

671
44:21.338 --> 44:22.368
You're distracting me.

672
44:27.008 --> 44:28.438
Why does it have to be so darn far?

673
44:47.128 --> 44:50.568
(Emergency Dispatch)

674
44:52.768 --> 44:54.798
(The Perfect Cleaning Experts: Clean Team)

675
45:03.778 --> 45:05.678
- Oh, no. What do we do? - Hey!

676
45:16.018 --> 45:17.058
Jun Seo.

677
45:18.158 --> 45:19.158
Jun Seo.

678
45:22.728 --> 45:23.728
Hey, Han Jun Seo!

679
45:27.998 --> 45:29.298
Jun Seo.

680
45:29.638 --> 45:30.638
Hey!

681
45:38.878 --> 45:39.878
Jun Seo.

682
45:40.878 --> 45:41.878
Jun Seo.

683
45:47.718 --> 45:50.258
- Oh, no. Call for help, quickly. - What do we do?

684
45:53.428 --> 45:54.498
Nam Il.

685
45:55.928 --> 45:56.928
Nam Il.

686
45:58.668 --> 45:59.998
Jun Seo.

687
46:00.438 --> 46:02.268
- Jun Seo. - Jun Seo.

688
46:02.268 --> 46:04.138
- Hey. - Hey, you punk.

689
46:04.608 --> 46:07.008
Jun Seo. Why is this punk's face so swollen?

690
46:07.178 --> 46:08.808
- Hey! - Hey, are you okay?

691
46:11.178 --> 46:12.248
Who are you?

692
46:13.118 --> 46:14.448
Hey, cut.

693
46:15.378 --> 46:16.988
- Hey, who are those guys? - I'm sorry.

694
46:17.188 --> 46:18.818
- Who are you guys? - Civilians.

695
46:18.918 --> 46:21.188
Can't you idiots control the crowd properly?

696
46:21.358 --> 46:23.228
Why did you let them drag you out?

697
46:23.228 --> 46:25.988
I thought they were other actors, so I just went with it.

698
46:26.428 --> 46:27.428
Unbelievable.

699
46:28.228 --> 46:29.258
- We're sorry. - We're sorry.

700
46:31.698 --> 46:34.538
- Go. - Do we go?

701
46:35.698 --> 46:37.168
- We're sorry. - We're sorry.

702
46:39.468 --> 46:41.238
Unbelievable.

703
46:42.238 --> 46:43.278
Hey, wrap it up.

704
46:51.248 --> 46:52.718
Why would I kill myself?

705
46:53.258 --> 46:54.258
Exactly, you punk.

706
46:54.618 --> 46:55.888
Who told you to vanish without a word?

707
46:56.258 --> 46:58.028
Then why did you turn off your phone?

708
46:58.088 --> 46:59.388
Are you going through an emo phase or something?

709
47:00.758 --> 47:02.098
Did you really have to jump to that conclusion?

710
47:02.958 --> 47:04.668
You should have checked who it was before diving in.

711
47:05.068 --> 47:07.068
I tell you to think before you act...

712
47:07.168 --> 47:08.168
so many times.

713
47:11.638 --> 47:12.708
Should I kill this punk?

714
47:13.008 --> 47:14.278
Yes, let's kill him.

715
47:14.578 --> 47:15.938
- Come here. Hey. - Hey.

716
47:16.378 --> 47:19.008
Sit down. You'll catch a cold. Hey.

717
47:19.778 --> 47:22.218
Sit down. Okay.

718
47:22.278 --> 47:23.988
- All right. - I'm hot, you jerk.

719
47:24.348 --> 47:25.548
- You're hot? - I'm fine.

720
47:25.618 --> 47:26.818
- If you're hot, bundle up more. - Darn it.

721
47:37.568 --> 47:38.968
Have you been here for two days?

722
47:40.598 --> 47:41.598
Yes.

723
47:44.868 --> 47:47.278
Why? Because you hate me?

724
47:57.688 --> 47:58.748
It's not that I hate you.

725
48:00.418 --> 48:02.658
I just wanted to run away for a bit.

726
48:06.258 --> 48:07.728
I knew it was all over,

727
48:09.928 --> 48:11.128
but when it actually hit,

728
48:13.668 --> 48:14.898
I couldn't handle it.

729
48:16.808 --> 48:19.738
So I thought, "Forget it. Let's just bail."

730
48:21.238 --> 48:23.148
"Then they won't be able to do anything either."

731
48:25.078 --> 48:26.108
That's what I thought.

732
48:26.178 --> 48:29.578
- You blockhead. - Total blockhead.

733
48:34.988 --> 48:36.018
You know,

734
48:37.528 --> 48:39.628
I have some serious grudges tied to this place.

735
48:42.158 --> 48:43.268
On our school trip,

736
48:43.928 --> 48:45.898
you two performed without me.

737
48:47.568 --> 48:48.598
It was so annoying.

738
48:48.938 --> 48:52.468
- What? When Man Sik punished us? - After that,

739
48:52.468 --> 48:54.308
we got beaten to a pulp.

740
48:55.608 --> 48:57.478
Do you guys remember the day we first met?

741
48:58.648 --> 48:59.918
- No. - No.

742
49:01.778 --> 49:03.048
I remember everything.

743
49:07.788 --> 49:08.988
Looking back,

744
49:09.758 --> 49:11.588
I think I liked you guys right from the start.

745
49:13.528 --> 49:16.358
Give me a break. Gosh.

746
49:17.968 --> 49:19.628
Cringe all you want.

747
49:21.438 --> 49:23.308
- It is the truth. - Oh, my.

748
49:24.638 --> 49:26.338
You know, this is something...

749
49:27.278 --> 49:28.308
I was going to take to my grave...

750
49:28.378 --> 49:31.108
- because it was so embarrassing. - Then keep it to yourself!

751
49:33.448 --> 49:35.478
The day we prepared for the broadcasting festival,

752
49:35.948 --> 49:37.888
I acted like I was just stuck hanging around,

753
49:38.848 --> 49:39.988
but that was not true.

754
49:40.488 --> 49:43.728
Darn it, how could you say yes without asking me?

755
49:43.858 --> 49:45.628
Do you think she will fall for you just because of this?

756
49:45.688 --> 49:46.698
Whatever.

757
49:46.758 --> 49:49.298
It is not like I said yes because of Lee Na Yeon.

758
49:49.758 --> 49:50.868
Oh, really?

759
49:50.968 --> 49:52.998
You crazy jerk. When did you even memorize her name?

760
49:56.808 --> 49:59.438
I will contact the school, so just come out.

761
50:00.478 --> 50:02.808
That day, I had a private tutoring session...

762
50:02.838 --> 50:03.948
that cost 1,000 dollars an hour.

763
50:04.148 --> 50:07.148
My dad told me to come out, but I ignored him.

764
50:08.018 --> 50:10.048
Because I wanted to stay with you guys longer.

765
50:11.818 --> 50:13.858
I got in so much trouble that day.

766
50:15.388 --> 50:17.558
Jun Seo, if it was 1,000 dollars an hour,

767
50:17.628 --> 50:20.758
- should you not have gone? - You nutjob.

768
50:21.398 --> 50:22.428
Right?

769
50:28.498 --> 50:30.068
It was my choice, Tae Gu.

770
50:35.608 --> 50:37.148
I was never smart...

771
50:38.008 --> 50:39.148
like my father or my brother,

772
50:40.018 --> 50:41.318
nor was I ambitious,

773
50:43.388 --> 50:45.718
so I spent my whole life trying to pretend.

774
50:48.958 --> 50:50.588
Pretending I wanted to go to a top college.

775
50:52.888 --> 50:54.158
Pretending I was fine being alone.

776
50:58.198 --> 50:59.268
You were the first...

777
51:00.938 --> 51:02.038
to see right through me.

778
51:06.708 --> 51:08.238
People who do not know anything...

779
51:09.878 --> 51:12.378
keep saying that you ruined my future.

780
51:16.618 --> 51:17.818
I want to give comedy a shot.

781
51:19.218 --> 51:21.718
Seriously, for real.

782
51:22.818 --> 51:25.058
- You want to do what? - Just ten years.

783
51:26.188 --> 51:27.858
Let us give it our all for ten years,

784
51:28.698 --> 51:30.228
and if it does not work out, I will walk away clean.

785
51:31.028 --> 51:32.068
So...

786
51:35.438 --> 51:36.538
guys...

787
51:39.308 --> 51:40.508
Do you want to do this with me?

788
51:45.308 --> 51:47.148
Next is the clinical approach...

789
51:47.378 --> 51:48.818
for patients presenting with proteinuria.

790
51:49.318 --> 51:51.948
The evaluation of proteinuria typically begins...

791
51:51.948 --> 51:55.218
with a positive result on a urine dipstick test.

792
51:55.658 --> 51:58.288
The dipstick test detects albumin,

793
51:58.358 --> 52:00.028
and the quantity of albumin is simply reported...

794
52:00.098 --> 52:04.198
as one plus, two plus, or three plus.

795
52:08.998 --> 52:10.008
I know.

796
52:12.568 --> 52:13.578
When you...

797
52:14.978 --> 52:16.608
asked me to do comedy with you,

798
52:20.118 --> 52:22.248
it was not really because you needed me.

799
52:30.828 --> 52:33.828
You reached out to give me...

800
52:36.028 --> 52:37.398
a way to run away.

801
52:50.148 --> 52:52.848
Hey, if it weren't for you guys,

802
52:54.118 --> 52:55.848
I would've died a long time ago.

803
53:17.538 --> 53:18.608
Tae Gu.

804
53:21.978 --> 53:23.908
You didn't steal ten years from me.

805
53:26.008 --> 53:28.248
You gave me ten more years to live, Tae Gu.

806
53:50.368 --> 53:51.368
I was scared.

807
53:56.738 --> 53:58.778
I was scared you guys would regret meeting me.

808
54:02.278 --> 54:03.318
You crazy idiot.

809
54:05.118 --> 54:07.918
Is that why you acted...

810
54:09.488 --> 54:12.358
like such a fool? You useless jerk.

811
54:15.828 --> 54:19.498
I don't want us to split up.

812
54:21.268 --> 54:23.668
I want to keep going together a little longer.

813
54:27.538 --> 54:30.508
Me neither. I don't want to split up either.

814
54:31.548 --> 54:34.518
I know it's ridiculous of me to say this...

815
54:35.878 --> 54:38.548
after being the first one to say we should quit.

816
54:43.288 --> 54:46.288
That's why I was holding back.

817
54:47.498 --> 54:49.658
Our ten years...

818
54:51.228 --> 54:53.128
I hate having them laughed at...

819
54:55.168 --> 54:56.168
like this.

820
54:57.368 --> 54:58.768
Just one last time,

821
55:00.008 --> 55:01.908
I want to try just one more time.

822
55:05.248 --> 55:06.278
Can't we?

823
55:10.488 --> 55:13.818
- Just once. - Just once.

824
55:13.858 --> 55:15.588
- Just once. - Just once.

825
55:16.088 --> 55:17.358
- Just once. - Just once.

826
55:18.028 --> 55:20.088
Why isn't this kid here yet?

827
55:20.598 --> 55:22.658
None of these punks take their boss seriously.

828
55:22.728 --> 55:23.968
I should just fire them all.

829
55:24.928 --> 55:27.368
Sir, you missed a spot here.

830
55:28.538 --> 55:29.568
Darn it.

831
55:32.138 --> 55:33.168
I won't do it again.

832
55:36.078 --> 55:37.108
I'm sorry.

833
55:38.278 --> 55:39.408
Wipe that smirk off your face.

834
55:39.478 --> 55:41.218
It's annoying.

835
55:42.948 --> 55:43.988
By the way, sir,

836
55:45.148 --> 55:46.548
how did you know I was there?

837
55:50.988 --> 55:52.288
You knew from the beginning, didn't you?

838
55:53.958 --> 55:55.028
How bad I was.

839
55:57.268 --> 55:58.968
That's why you set me up with them, right?

840
56:00.468 --> 56:01.698
Because they're good kids,

841
56:02.838 --> 56:04.408
you knew they'd take me in.

842
56:06.208 --> 56:09.238
From what I've seen in life, not everyone is born...

843
56:09.308 --> 56:10.808
where they rightly belong.

844
56:12.078 --> 56:14.618
I set you up, sure, but you chose to fit in with them.

845
56:15.748 --> 56:17.048
That was where you belonged.

846
56:19.288 --> 56:21.288
You're a good kid too, you punk.

847
56:21.958 --> 56:23.318
It's not just them.

848
56:30.128 --> 56:31.128
Mr. Jung.

849
56:37.938 --> 56:40.408
You need to wipe down all of this water again.

850
56:40.738 --> 56:41.738
What will you do with all this water?

851
56:41.808 --> 56:44.508
What are you even wiping?

852
56:45.108 --> 56:46.348
Seriously.

853
56:48.718 --> 56:49.718
Gosh.

854
56:49.778 --> 56:51.448
So Tae Gu still hasn't come around?

855
56:53.348 --> 56:55.388
Yes. Well, it was a hard decision for him to make,

856
56:55.888 --> 56:57.288
so reversing it must not be easy.

857
56:59.288 --> 57:01.258
You know how stubborn he can be.

858
57:03.968 --> 57:04.968
Still,

859
57:06.828 --> 57:08.198
I'm going to wait for him until the end.

860
57:12.838 --> 57:14.708
We always eat nothing but junk food.

861
57:14.778 --> 57:16.378
Let's eat something else for a change.

862
57:16.438 --> 57:17.978
Yes, let's get some meat.

863
57:18.348 --> 57:19.348
Let's do that.

864
57:19.508 --> 57:20.518
- When? - When?

865
57:21.378 --> 57:24.818
- Later. - Man, what a buzz kill.

866
57:24.818 --> 57:26.588
Green onions are more expensive these days.

867
57:26.818 --> 57:28.088
What is this? Hey, you...

868
57:28.988 --> 57:30.428
Hey, what should we have for dinner tonight?

869
57:31.258 --> 57:32.858
- Hey! - Yes?

870
57:32.928 --> 57:34.528
I told you not to waste toilet paper!

871
57:35.658 --> 57:38.098
- He started it! - Did I not tell you not to use it?

872
57:38.168 --> 57:39.568
- Hey, Jun Seo, look at this. - I told you to stop!

873
57:39.628 --> 57:41.798
- Hey, look at this. Look. - What is that? Who was it?

874
57:41.868 --> 57:43.808
- It was him. - Who was it? Who?

875
57:43.868 --> 57:45.608
- Was it you? Who was it? - It was not me.

876
57:45.668 --> 57:46.738
No, I did not do that at all.

877
57:50.078 --> 57:51.178
Hey.

878
57:54.718 --> 57:56.718
Hey, are you not going to clean?

879
57:56.978 --> 57:59.548
- I won the bet. - What bet?

880
58:00.458 --> 58:05.058
All right, here you go. Careful, it is hot.

881
58:08.758 --> 58:10.798
- That is fun. - You think so?

882
58:13.498 --> 58:14.738
It tastes a bit strange.

883
58:15.798 --> 58:17.968
Hey, no one could be as desperate as you.

884
58:18.608 --> 58:20.378
Were you not rejected by Na Yeon a hundred times?

885
58:20.408 --> 58:21.838
It was 99... Oh, come on.

886
58:24.848 --> 58:26.448
- What are you doing? - What do I do?

887
58:26.508 --> 58:28.378
Let us do that. Hey, let us use that later.

888
58:30.918 --> 58:34.658
Hey, Jun Seo, can you see my underwear?

889
58:35.488 --> 58:36.488
- No. - Is it okay? Am I good?

890
58:36.558 --> 58:37.628
Yes, you are fine.

891
58:37.688 --> 58:39.128
- Are you sure? - Yes.

892
58:39.288 --> 58:40.758
Hey, what was that bit we changed?

893
58:41.298 --> 58:42.558
When I point to the seats on the left...

894
58:42.628 --> 58:44.368
- When you point left. - The seats.

895
58:44.428 --> 58:46.728
- When I point there. - Okay. Got it.

896
58:46.798 --> 58:48.198
- Okay. Got it. - Okay.

897
58:50.968 --> 58:53.638
- Let's go. All right. - Guys.

898
58:53.668 --> 58:54.708
- Pardon? - You are up next.

899
58:54.978 --> 58:56.338
- Okay, let us go. - Let us go.

900
59:00.378 --> 59:01.378
Guys.

901
59:06.448 --> 59:07.488
Is it...

902
59:12.628 --> 59:13.628
really okay?

903
59:17.498 --> 59:18.598
Of course it is, you idiot.

904
59:29.638 --> 59:30.648
Then...

905
59:33.108 --> 59:34.448
I want to try one more time.

906
59:39.788 --> 59:40.858
Let us take it all the way.

907
59:43.158 --> 59:44.158
Together.

908
59:53.468 --> 59:55.338
What? Let go! Stop it, I said!

909
59:55.698 --> 59:56.998
Was it really that hard on you?

910
59:57.768 --> 59:59.808
- Come on, please? - You little punk.

911
59:59.868 --> 01:00:02.838
- Hey, are we doing the show or not? - You were crying, were you not?

912
01:00:02.978 --> 01:00:04.208
- I was not. - You totally cried.

913
01:00:04.278 --> 01:00:05.848
- I said I did not cry! - He cried. I saw him cry.

914
01:00:05.978 --> 01:00:07.418
- You saw what? - I saw you.

915
01:00:07.448 --> 01:00:09.218
- You are tearing up. - I am not crying. It is too spicy,

916
01:00:09.278 --> 01:00:10.278
that is why.

917
01:00:10.348 --> 01:00:12.388
- Give me a break. Spicy, my foot. - I did not cry, jerk.

918
